# Weather provider configuration
#
# The app uses Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com) by default — it requires
# NO API key for this app's usage level, so there is nothing to configure
# to get real weather working out of the box, and no secret is ever bundled
# into the GitHub Pages build.
#
# If you swap in a keyed provider later (e.g. OpenWeatherMap), copy this
# file to `.env.local` (already gitignored — never commit a real key) and
# set:
#
# VITE_WEATHER_API_KEY=your-key-here
#
# Then read it in src/lib/weather.ts via `import.meta.env.VITE_WEATHER_API_KEY`
# and pass it into that provider's request. Vite only exposes variables
# prefixed `VITE_` to client code — by definition anything here ends up
# visible in the shipped JS bundle, so only ever put a key here that's safe
# to expose client-side (a public/rate-limited key, not a billing-linked
# secret). Nothing outside lib/weather.ts needs to change either way.
